From 50fdc94decd6725adece2877c868bcb02e95c582 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: stefanoconiglio <33290924+stefanoconiglio@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 06:07:30 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 18/19] pdf:content and pdf:literal specials are drawn; a clip
 left open no longer kills TeXpresso

trimclip's XeTeX driver (adjustbox's clip) clips a box with
"pdf:content q", a "pdf:code ... re W n" clip path, the box, then two
"pdf:literal direct Q". Only pdf:code was known: the clip was opened and
never closed, and the device the page was drawn to threw "items left on
stack in draw device" on closing, which no fz_try caught: TeXpresso died
("aborting process from uncaught error!").

pdf:content OPS now runs OPS as pdf:code does, between a q and a Q (as
dvipdfmx writes it, OPS drawn at the current point), and pdf:literal
[direct] OPS as pdf:code. The two are matched by plain C ahead of the
re2c rules, so dvi_special.c carries the same lines without being
generated again.

At the end of a frame, the clips the page left open are popped from the
device, with a line on stderr, so a document that opens a clip and never
closes it shows its page instead.
---
 src/dvi/dvi_context.c      |  13 +++
 src/dvi/dvi_special.c      | 179 ++++++++++++++++++++++++-------------
 src/dvi/dvi_special.re2c.c |  55 ++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 185 insertions(+), 62 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/dvi/dvi_context.c b/src/dvi/dvi_context.c
index 4045ab1..434324a 100644
--- a/src/dvi/dvi_context.c
+++ b/src/dvi/dvi_context.c
@@ -84,6 +84,19 @@ void dvi_context_begin_frame(fz_context *ctx, dvi_context *dc, fz_device *dev)
 void dvi_context_end_frame(fz_context *ctx, dvi_context *dc)
 {
   dvi_scratch_clear(ctx, &dc->scratch);
+
+  // A clip the page opened and never closed would be left on the stack of
+  // the device the page is drawn to, which then refuses to close.
+  dvi_state *st = &dc->root;
+  if (st->gs.clip_depth > 0)
+  {
+    fprintf(stderr, "ending frame with %d clips open\n", st->gs.clip_depth);
+    if (dc->dev)
+      for (int i = 0; i < st->gs.clip_depth; ++i)
+        fz_pop_clip(ctx, dc->dev);
+    st->gs.clip_depth = 0;
+  }
+
   dvi_context_set_device(ctx, dc, NULL);
 
   if (dc->colorstack.depth > 0)
diff --git a/src/dvi/dvi_special.c b/src/dvi/dvi_special.c
index 516e30d..a8004a9 100644
